      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a 2022 F-150 with a slipping issue. my scan tool is showing some really weird irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. what are the most likely things causing pressure fluctuations like that in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those irregular pressure spikes in your 2022 F-150's transmission are most likely caused by a failing torque converter clutch solenoid, a clogged or contaminated valve body, or a weak torque converter itself. Since the transmission control module relies on these components to manage clutch apply pressures, any mechanical weakness or electrical glitch can create the erratic behavior your scan tool is detecting. You should also inspect the transmission fluid for metal shavings or wrong viscosity, as poor fluid condition often exacerbates solenoid stalling and pressure surges.",
