      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given that your fluid is clean and external components check out, the fluctuations are likely due to worn internal stator one-ways inside the torque converter or shifting gears where the hydraulic pressure is critically dependent on a single small component. You might also have an internal valve seat issue that isn't visible from outside or a minor dash valve blockage developing over time. A specialized diagnostic of the input and output shaft speeds could reveal if the issue stems from the converter's integrate behavior rather than the valve body itself.",
