      "content": "The random, \"ghost-like\" behavior often points to issues with the transmission output shaft speed sensor or the vehicle speed sensor sending inconsistent data to the ECM. Since dust or wear can affect these specific mounts intermittently, the PCM may misjudge load tolerance and react unpredictably on specific shifts. Another possibility is a failing modulator valve or an internal clutch pack that is hard to map without starting a vibration analysis on the transmission case itself.",
